Delegating to the skill gave me the concrete rules I'm applying: 48dp/44pt minimum touch targets, no truncated text (rows grow instead), destructive action confirmed via a two-action dialog (`Alert.alert` with a `destructive` style button — satisfies both iOS's "alert for something the user must know now" and Android's "dialog has at most two actions"), and the tonal dark-mode elevation ladder instead of hard-coded hex values. Here's the complete screen as a single self-contained file (React Native + TypeScript, no extra dependencies beyond `react` / `react-native`):

```tsx
// AccountSettingsScreen.tsx
import React, { useMemo, useState, useCallback } from 'react';
import {
  View,
  Text,
  Pressable,
  Switch,
  ScrollView,
  SafeAreaView,
  Alert,
  ActivityIndicator,
  useColorScheme,
  StyleSheet,
  Image,
} from 'react-native';

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Design tokens — semantic roles, aliased to a light/dark primitive scale.
// Dark mode follows the "nearer surface = lighter" elevation ladder, not
// shadows: bg.app (0) < bg.surface (1) < bg.surface-raised (2) ...
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
const lightTokens = {
  bgApp: '#F2F2F7',
  bgSurface: '#FFFFFF',
  borderSubtle: '#E3E3E8',
  textPrimary: '#1C1C1E',
  textMuted: '#6B6B70',
  accentSolid: '#2F6FED',
  dangerText: '#D92D20',
  onSurface: '#1C1C1E',
};

const darkTokens = {
  bgApp: '#0E0E10',       // level 0 — darkest, avoid pure black
  bgSurface: '#1C1C1E',   // level 1 — cards / rows, lighter than app bg
  borderSubtle: '#2F2F33',
  textPrimary: '#F2F2F3',
  textMuted: '#9B9BA1',
  accentSolid: '#5B8DEF',
  dangerText: '#FF6961',
  onSurface: '#F2F2F3',
};

type Tokens = typeof lightTokens;

function useTokens(): Tokens {
  const scheme = useColorScheme();
  return scheme === 'dark' ? darkTokens : lightTokens;
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Shared row primitive — enforces the 48dp/44pt minimum touch target on both
// platforms, lets content grow instead of truncating at large text sizes,
// and exposes an accessible role/label for screen readers.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
const MIN_TARGET = 48;

function Row({
  tokens,
  label,
  sublabel,
  onPress,
  accessory,
  destructive,
  disabled,
  accessibilityLabel,
}: {
  tokens: Tokens;
  label: string;
  sublabel?: string;
  onPress?: () => void;
  accessory?: React.ReactNode;
  destructive?: boolean;
  disabled?: boolean;
  accessibilityLabel?: string;
}) {
  const textColor = destructive ? tokens.dangerText : tokens.textPrimary;

  return (
    <Pressable
      onPress={onPress}
      disabled={disabled || !onPress}
      accessibilityRole={onPress ? 'button' : undefined}
      accessibilityLabel={accessibilityLabel ?? label}
      accessibilityState={{ disabled: !!disabled }}
      style={({ pressed }) => [
        styles.row,
        { minHeight: MIN_TARGET, backgroundColor: tokens.bgSurface },
        pressed && onPress ? { opacity: 0.6 } : null,
      ]}
    >
      <View style={styles.rowTextBlock}>
        <Text style={[styles.rowLabel, { color: textColor }]}>{label}</Text>
        {sublabel ? (
          <Text style={[styles.rowSublabel, { color: tokens.textMuted }]}>
            {sublabel}
          </Text>
        ) : null}
      </View>
      {disabled ? (
        <ActivityIndicator size="small" color={tokens.textMuted} />
      ) : (
        accessory
      )}
    </Pressable>
  );
}

function Chevron({ tokens }: { tokens: Tokens }) {
  return <Text style={{ color: tokens.textMuted, fontSize: 20 }}>{'\u203A'}</Text>;
}

function SectionHeader({ tokens, title }: { tokens: Tokens; title: string }) {
  return (
    <Text style={[styles.sectionHeader, { color: tokens.textMuted }]}>{title}</Text>
  );
}

function Section({
  tokens,
  children,
}: {
  tokens: Tokens;
  children: React.ReactNode;
}) {
  return (
    <View
      style={[
        styles.section,
        { backgroundColor: tokens.bgSurface, borderColor: tokens.borderSubtle },
      ]}
    >
      {children}
    </View>
  );
}

function Divider({ tokens }: { tokens: Tokens }) {
  return <View style={[styles.divider, { backgroundColor: tokens.borderSubtle }]} />;
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Public screen
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
export type AccountSettingsScreenProps = {
  user: {
    name: string;
    email: string;
    avatarUrl?: string;
  };
  onEditProfile: () => void;
  onOpenPrivacy: () => void;
  onOpenSecurity: () => void;
  onOpenHelp: () => void;
  onLogout: () => void;
  /** Called only after the user confirms the destructive dialog. Should reject on failure. */
  onDeleteAccount: () => Promise<void>;
};

export default function AccountSettingsScreen({
  user,
  onEditProfile,
  onOpenPrivacy,
  onOpenSecurity,
  onOpenHelp,
  onLogout,
  onDeleteAccount,
}: AccountSettingsScreenProps) {
  const tokens = useTokens();
  const [notificationsEnabled, setNotificationsEnabled] = useState(true);
  const [isDeleting, setIsDeleting] = useState(false);

  const initials = useMemo(
    () =>
      user.name
        .split(' ')
        .filter(Boolean)
        .slice(0, 2)
        .map((part) => part[0]?.toUpperCase())
        .join(''),
    [user.name]
  );

  const runDelete = useCallback(async () => {
    setIsDeleting(true);
    try {
      await onDeleteAccount();
    } catch (err) {
      Alert.alert(
        'Couldn’t delete account',
        'Something went wrong. Please check your connection and try again.'
      );
    } finally {
      setIsDeleting(false);
    }
  }, [onDeleteAccount]);

  const confirmDelete = useCallback(() => {
    // Two-action dialog: Cancel + a single destructive-styled confirm, per
    // platform guidance (iOS: destructive alert style; Android: at most two
    // dialog actions, one confirms, one dismisses).
    Alert.alert(
      'Delete account?',
      'This permanently deletes your account and all of your data. This action can’t be undone.',
      [
        { text: 'Cancel', style: 'cancel' },
        { text: 'Delete', style: 'destructive', onPress: runDelete },
      ],
      { cancelable: true }
    );
  }, [runDelete]);

  return (
    <SafeAreaView style={[styles.safeArea, { backgroundColor: tokens.bgApp }]}>
      <ScrollView
        contentContainerStyle={styles.scrollContent}
        contentInsetAdjustmentBehavior="automatic"
      >
        {/* Profile row */}
        <Section tokens={tokens}>
          <Pressable
            onPress={onEditProfile}
            accessibilityRole="button"
            accessibilityLabel={`Edit profile, ${user.name}, ${user.email}`}
            style={({ pressed }) => [
              styles.profileRow,
              { minHeight: 64 },
              pressed ? { opacity: 0.6 } : null,
            ]}
          >
            {user.avatarUrl ? (
              <Image source={{ uri: user.avatarUrl }} style={styles.avatar} />
            ) : (
              <View
                style={[styles.avatar, styles.avatarFallback, { backgroundColor: tokens.accentSolid }]}
              >
                <Text style={styles.avatarInitials}>{initials}</Text>
              </View>
            )}
            <View style={styles.rowTextBlock}>
              <Text style={[styles.profileName, { color: tokens.textPrimary }]}>
                {user.name}
              </Text>
              <Text style={[styles.rowSublabel, { color: tokens.textMuted }]}>
                {user.email}
              </Text>
            </View>
            <Chevron tokens={tokens} />
          </Pressable>
        </Section>

        {/* Settings rows */}
        <SectionHeader tokens={tokens} title="PREFERENCES" />
        <Section tokens={tokens}>
          <Row
            tokens={tokens}
            label="Notifications"
            accessory={
              <Switch
                value={notificationsEnabled}
                onValueChange={setNotificationsEnabled}
                trackColor={{ false: tokens.borderSubtle, true: tokens.accentSolid }}
                accessibilityLabel="Notifications"
                accessibilityRole="switch"
              />
            }
          />
          <Divider tokens={tokens} />
          <Row
            tokens={tokens}
            label="Privacy"
            onPress={onOpenPrivacy}
            accessory={<Chevron tokens={tokens} />}
          />
          <Divider tokens={tokens} />
          <Row
            tokens={tokens}
            label="Security"
            onPress={onOpenSecurity}
            accessory={<Chevron tokens={tokens} />}
          />
        </Section>

        <SectionHeader tokens={tokens} title="SUPPORT" />
        <Section tokens={tokens}>
          <Row
            tokens={tokens}
            label="Help & Support"
            onPress={onOpenHelp}
            accessory={<Chevron tokens={tokens} />}
          />
          <Divider tokens={tokens} />
          <Row tokens={tokens} label="Log Out" onPress={onLogout} />
        </Section>

        {/* Delete account — isolated in its own section, same pattern iOS/
            Android settings apps use to separate destructive actions. */}
        <SectionHeader tokens={tokens} title="ACCOUNT" />
        <Section tokens={tokens}>
          <Row
            tokens={tokens}
            label="Delete Account"
            onPress={confirmDelete}
            destructive
            disabled={isDeleting}
            accessibilityLabel="Delete account. Irreversible."
          />
        </Section>
      </ScrollView>
    </SafeAreaView>
  );
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Styles
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
const styles = StyleSheet.create({
  safeArea: {
    flex: 1,
  },
  scrollContent: {
    paddingVertical: 16,
    paddingHorizontal: 16,
    gap: 4,
  },
  section: {
    borderRadius: 12,
    borderWidth: 1,
    overflow: 'hidden',
    marginBottom: 20,
  },
  row: {
    flexDirection: 'row',
    alignItems: 'center',
    paddingHorizontal: 16,
    paddingVertical: 12,
    gap: 12,
  },
  rowTextBlock: {
    flex: 1,
    flexShrink: 1,
  },
  rowLabel: {
    fontSize: 16,
    fontWeight: '400',
  },
  rowSublabel: {
    fontSize: 13,
    marginTop: 2,
  },
  sectionHeader: {
    fontSize: 13,
    fontWeight: '600',
    marginBottom: 8,
    marginLeft: 4,
  },
  divider: {
    height: 1,
    marginLeft: 16,
  },
  profileRow: {
    flexDirection: 'row',
    alignItems: 'center',
    paddingHorizontal: 16,
    paddingVertical: 12,
    gap: 12,
  },
  avatar: {
    width: 48,
    height: 48,
    borderRadius: 24,
  },
  avatarFallback: {
    alignItems: 'center',
    justifyContent: 'center',
  },
  avatarInitials: {
    color: '#FFFFFF',
    fontSize: 18,
    fontWeight: '600',
  },
  profileName: {
    fontSize: 17,
    fontWeight: '600',
  },
});
```

Notes on the choices, tied back to the platform rules:

- **Touch targets** — every interactive row uses `minHeight: 48` (satisfies Android's 48dp floor and exceeds iOS's 44pt), and the row grows with content (`paddingVertical` + no fixed height, no `numberOfLines`) so it doesn't clip at large Dynamic Type / accessibility font sizes.
- **Delete confirmation** — a single `Alert.alert` with exactly two actions, `Cancel` and a `style: 'destructive'` confirm. This renders as iOS's destructive-red alert button and respects Android's "a dialog has at most two actions, one confirms, one dismisses" rule, without needing platform-forked code.
- **Dark mode** — colors come from semantic tokens (`bgApp`, `bgSurface`, `textPrimary`, `dangerText`, …), and the dark set lightens surfaces for nearer layers (`bgSurface` lighter than `bgApp`) rather than inverting or using shadows, per the elevation ladder.
- **Isolation of the destructive action** — Delete Account sits alone in its own trailing section, separated from Log Out and other settings, matching how both OSes visually quarantine destructive actions.
- **Accessibility** — rows carry `accessibilityRole`/`accessibilityLabel`, the switch is announced as a switch, and the delete row's label states irreversibility for screen reader users.
- Wire the five callback props (`onEditProfile`, `onOpenPrivacy`, `onOpenSecurity`, `onOpenHelp`, `onLogout`, `onDeleteAccount`) to your navigation/API layer — `onDeleteAccount` is expected to return a promise so the row can show a spinner and disable itself mid-request.
